<h1>Jawaharial &quot;Omar&quot; Williams</h1>
<p>Illinois House, 10th District, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Democratic. Incumbent.</p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>No campaign site found. His House Democratic caucus page describes his focus as improving access to health care, safer communities, and increasing economic prosperity; he chairs the House Prescription Drug Affordability Committee and has sponsored legislation expanding access to opioid overdose antagonists at concert venues.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Former laborer with the Chicago Department of Water Management and member of the Laborers&#39; International Union and Plumbers Local 130, and former president of the Young Democrats of Illinois; appointed to the House in May 2019.</p>
